```c
int ret;
ret = icl_calc_wrpll(crtc_state, &pll_params);
if (ret)
    return ret;
```
Reason:
Changing the type of `ret` from `bool` to `int` allows it to hold zero or negative error codes as intended. This ensures that when the function fails, it returns the appropriate error code, enabling correct error handling and interpretation of the function's status.

